  "section": "116",
  "quote": "A landlord shall not increase the rent charged to a tenant for a rental unit without first giving the tenant at least 90 days written notice of the landlord’s intention to do so.",
  "reason": "The clause allows the landlord to increase the rent with only 30 days' written notice, which conflicts with Section 116(1) requiring at least 90 days' written notice. Because the provision is inconsistent with the Act, it is void under Section 4(1)."
}

